<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2">
  <Document>
    <name>💨 LIVE WIND</name>
    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/wind_na_basin/legend.png?v=na-wind-20261014-0901-gdps-GDPS_15km_Wind_10m-n-5273396-glwu-20261014-07-n-13895-hrrr-hrrr.20261014-08-n-701862-rrfs-na-rrfs.20261014-00-n-2632946" width="600" alt="legend"><br>WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE (colors follow force, dark purple = Force 12 only). Speed m/s &rarr; kt (x1.94384) &rarr; WMO Beaufort 0-12. Arrows point TOWARD motion; calm (&lt;0.5 m/s) draws no arrow. Same force always shows the same color.</p><p><b>Status:</b> LIVE / CURRENT MODEL (analysis, GLWU + HRRR + RRFS-NA, GDPS fallback)</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/NCEP GLWU v2.1 surface U/V (Great Lakes water) + HRRR 3km 10m U/V + RRFS North American 10m U/V + ECCC GDPS fallback<br/><a href="https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_glwu.pl">https://nomads.ncep.noaa.gov/cgi-bin/filter_glwu.pl</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of all other layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>◉ <b>Great Lakes Basin Coverage</b> (this view)<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_Extended.kml">Extended North America Coverage</a><br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
    <Folder>
      <name>LIVE WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE — Great Lakes Basin Coverage</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<p>WIND — BEAUFORT SCALE (colors follow force, dark purple = Force 12 only). Speed m/s &rarr; kt (x1.94384) &rarr; WMO Beaufort 0-12. Arrows point TOWARD motion; calm (&lt;0.5 m/s) draws no arrow. Same force always shows the same color.</p><p><b>Coverage:</b> Great Lakes Basin Coverage<br><b>Precedence:</b> GLWU valid (Great Lakes water) > HRRR valid (its domain, GLWU not applicable) > RRFS-NA valid (elsewhere) > GDPS (verified gaps only) > transparent.<br><b>Provenance:</b> {'glwu 20261014/07': 'n=13895', 'hrrr hrrr.20261014/08': 'n=701862', 'rrfs-na rrfs.20261014/00': 'n=2632946', 'gdps': 'GDPS_15km_Wind_10m n=5273396'}</p><p><b>Coverage Selector</b> — one coverage at a time (Pro switches exclusively; Web/app: uncheck the others):<br>◉ <b>Great Lakes Basin Coverage</b> (this view)<br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_NorthAmerica.kml">North America Coverage</a><br>○ <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_Extended.kml">Extended North America Coverage</a><br>Add once: <a href="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/kml/North_America_Live_Wind_Coverage.kml">Coverage collection file</a> (all three as toggles).</p>]]></description>
